{
  "_comment": "Armoured stands, for pricing the entity layer renderers. entity-dense summons its 120 stands bare, so its armour layer runs over four empty slots and renders nothing — the counter that reads 4 pieces per entity there is counting slots, not armour. Each stand here wears a full diamond set and holds a sword, so LayerBipedArmor draws four models and LayerHeldItem one.\nDeterministic on purpose. replay-pit cannot do this job: its measured window is a wall-clock slice of a recording, so a slower run lands on a different replay position and sees a different crowd — three variants of one probe there drew 21.5, 23.0 and 24.9 entities a frame, a 16% spread that swamps what the probe is trying to measure.\nTimed like text-dense-quick so a three-way ceiling probe stays near the five-minute budget. Player slot 0 is left empty: a held item swings and dominates the pixel gate.",
